From: folia-linear-ci <30575805+Ashu11-A@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Linear save barrier: real save-all flush, save-off lease,
 durable player data

save-all is registered again on Folia (upstream left it as TODO) and runs
region by region: one tick task per owned region section, the first task
in a region saves that region's chunks (flush: storages go through the
forced Linear barrier) and then only that region's players, so a player
file is never written before its region's chunks. After the last task a
flush save-all runs the forced coordinator barrier off-thread and writes
<level>/linear-checkpoint/save-all.done {id,startMs,endMs,regions,failed}
atomically before reporting success. The periodic player autosave now
respects save-off (level.noSave), and a save-off older than
save-off-max-duration (default 120 s, 0 disables) turns saving back on
with a WARN and an ops broadcast. With durable-player-data (default true)
player .dat files are replaced by a .dat_old hard link and one
ATOMIC_MOVE (no fsync on the tick thread); stats and advancements are
replaced atomically; orphan temp files are quarantined at boot; every
.dat_old fallback logs a WARN.

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/configuration/GlobalConfiguration.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/configuration/GlobalConfiguration.java
index 6457e64de8a810e506bcdcd2f68036453234d534..3622e622b77fa7731019d390a9e11fb2140b11f3 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/configuration/GlobalConfiguration.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/configuration/GlobalConfiguration.java
@@ -366,9 +366,17 @@ public class GlobalConfiguration extends ConfigurationPart {
             public String implementation = "V1";
             @Comment("Bucket grid for V2/V3 writes: 1, 2, 4, 8 (default), 16 or 32. Off-list values log a warning and use 8. -Dlinearmc.grid-size wins.")
             public int gridSize = 8;
+            @Comment("Seconds a save-off may last before saving turns itself back on, with a WARN and an ops broadcast (default 120; 0 disables). Stops a backup client that died after save-off from freezing saves.")
+            public long saveOffMaxDuration = 120;
+            @Comment("Player .dat, stats and advancements: one atomic rename, .dat_old kept as the previous save, orphan temp files quarantined at boot (default true). No fsync on the tick thread; coupled-save writes are forced and directory-synced off-thread. Same bytes as vanilla; false restores the vanilla replace.")
+            public boolean durablePlayerData = true;
 
             @PostProcess
             private void postProcess() {
+                // Linear - save barrier keys, published to the core once per config load.
+                this.saveOffMaxDuration = net.linear.save.SaveOffLease.resolveMaxDurationSeconds(this.saveOffMaxDuration, LOGGER::error);
+                net.linear.save.SaveOffLease.setMaxDurationSeconds(this.saveOffMaxDuration);
+                net.linear.io.PlayerFileDurability.setEnabled(this.durablePlayerData);
                 if (this.flushFrequency < 1) {
                     LOGGER.error("[region-format] linear.flush-frequency must be >= 1, got {}. Falling back to 10.", this.flushFrequency);
                     this.flushFrequency = 10;
